{
  "_comment": [
    "CANONICAL cross-repo fixtures for the reproducibility receipt (§3.13).",
    "",
    "Run through BOTH implementations:",
    "  - MCP app: server/receipt.ts (tests/unit/receipt-parity.test.ts)",
    "  - Website: index.html page globals (verify-parity.mjs)",
    "",
    "The FINGERPRINT values below are pinned deliberately. They are the interface",
    "between a receipt saved today and a re-run months later, and between the two",
    "repos — if either changes its digest, receipts already written down in someone's",
    "methods section stop matching. Changing the algorithm is a breaking change and",
    "these numbers are what make that visible.",
    "",
    "The load-bearing DIFF case is `refuses to compare two different searches`. Two",
    "different searches returning different totals is not a finding, and reporting it",
    "as 'N new records since July' would be the most plausible-looking wrong answer",
    "this feature could produce.",
    "",
    "On the pinned values: the empty / 'a' / 'b' cases are the independently",
    "documented FNV-1a 32-bit results, so they verify the ALGORITHM rather than",
    "ratifying whatever this code happens to emit. The remaining values were then",
    "computed from that verified implementation."
  ],
